// The time-zone tables and the offset lookup — the PLACEHOLDER (0.0.1 P-7).
//
// EMPTY ON PURPOSE: see `../core/core.npk` for why a placeholder exists at all.
// It is REPLACED at the cycles below, never deleted.
//
// WHAT FILLS IT: the four GENERATED flat tables and the name pool (cycle 0.5),
// then the transition binary search, the POSIX-rule extrapolation and the four
// resolution modes (cycle 0.6). Governed by `meta/specs/ZONE_MODEL.md`.
// WHEN: cycle 0.5 (`meta/roadmap/0.5/README.md`), then 0.6.
//
// THE GENERATED FILES BESIDE THIS ONE ARE SOURCE, and `.gitignore` says so
// explicitly: a build must need only the compiler — never a Python generator,
// never a network fetch, and never `/usr/share/zoneinfo` (TM-007, TM-027).
// `tools/gen_tzdb.py` regenerates them and the harness checks the committed
// tables are byte-identical to what it would emit (`BUILD.md` B-4).
//
// WHAT IT MAY IMPORT: `span`, `cal` and `core` (`BUILD.md` B-17). No hash map:
// the lookup is a binary search over a sorted index (B-13, `ZONE_MODEL.md`
// Z-9), which at 447 entries beats a hash and has one invariant instead of
// four.
//
// THE ERROR IT DECLARES: `ETimeZone`, the second of the three (TM-017).
mod:zone;
